WEBVTT

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:04.870
"Natural"?

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.790
What the heck?

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:07.500
Why?

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.500
Is it because I'm the leader?!

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.920
Screw it!

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.890
I quit being an idol!

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.390
Mio, are you serious?

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:24.640
...Mio...

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:27.650
...I mean, I...

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:33.150
Mio's coming today, right?

00:00:34.610 --> 00:00:36.680
She's not really quitting, right?

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.060
...Producer...

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.410
Hey... Mio isn't here yet.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:52.070
It seems so.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:53.840
That's it?

00:00:55.870 --> 00:00:57.330
...U-Um...

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.870
I'm thinking of going to Mio's house.

00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:04.740
Where does she live?

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.730
...Please...

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.810
Allow me to handle this.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.990
Mio... didn't come in today?

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:25.060
Maybe she's worn out from the mini-concert?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.710
Is Mio quitting?

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:34.300
Does that mean New Generations
is breaking up?!

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:36.800
...They debuted just yesterday too...

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.550
I meown't stand for this!

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:44.470
...She debuted before us, but meow—

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:46.530
Rin?!

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.520
Shibuya, are you okay?

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:49.410
Y-Yes.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:12.840
Sis.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.630
There's a guy calling himself
your producer out front.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.700
Tell him to go away.

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:20.340
Tell him yourself.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.470
I don't want to talk.

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.930
And don't come back here.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.480
...It'll only take a minute. Please—

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:34.610
I said, I don't want to talk.

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:36.610
Go away.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:42.860
Everyone's waiting for you.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.500
...This isn't only about you—

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.290
I know that!

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:56.870
Producer!

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:58.510
Did you see Mio?

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:02.550
She turned you away?

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:05.540
...Um...

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:09.410
I'd really like to pay Mio a visit.

00:03:10.270 --> 00:03:12.300
What's her address?

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.690
I can't give it to you.

00:03:15.830 --> 00:03:16.740
Why not?

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.810
Honda said that she didn't want to talk.

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:24.540
I'd like to uphold her wish if possible.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.200
And that's fine by you?

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.410
I have a meeting.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:31.690
Hey, wait!

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.510
Can we really leave this to him?

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:44.710
Uzuki?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.010
Huh?

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.140
Is something wrong?

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.720
Oh, sorry.

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:53.830
It's been a busy week.
Maybe I'm just tired.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.590
Oh.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:23.590
You're the first one here today.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.610
Uzuki isn't here.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.350
She called just a moment ago.

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.730
She's not feeling well
and will be taking the day off.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:54.650
What about Mio?

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:58.770
She hasn't called yet.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.630
What's going to happen to us?

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.890
What if Mio doesn't come back?

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.720
...I'll adjust the plans—

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:15.010
"Adjust"?

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:15.930
What's that mean?

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:17.930
...Um...

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.820
Please do what you can for now.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:25.940
I can't.

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.930
Look at the mess we're in.

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:31.890
What are you going to do about it?

00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.620
It'd better be something I can get behind.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.710
I admit that there's a difference of opinion.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.870
What good is that going to do <i>now</i>?!

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:43.920
Why don't you go and drag Mio back?!

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:49.050
Because she's not ready to come back yet.

00:05:54.010 --> 00:05:55.250
Don't run away.

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.150
...You told me...

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:04.820
that I'd find a whole new world
waiting for me here.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.360
...When I first stood on a stage...

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.390
...When I first heard our finished song...

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.370
I felt like I'd almost found it.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:17.660
Something I could devote myself to.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:20.710
...But now...

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.170
I feel like I never will.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:26.410
Tell me.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.460
What's this "difference of opinion"?

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.610
Why won't you bring Mio back?

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:39.260
What on Earth are you thinking?

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:44.190
I'm very sorry.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:50.270
...I thought I could trust you too...

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.280
Rin?

00:06:57.910 --> 00:07:00.000
What do you mean, she left?!

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.620
...We didn't get a chance to talk...

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:06.360
I' looks like Uzuki's ou' to'ay too.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:11.930
...Maybe they really <i>are</i> breaking up...

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:16.760
I shouldn't have invited them to my concert.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:19.330
What do we do, Sis?!

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:22.520
What did your producer say?

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:25.270
Nothing.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:29.530
We have no idea <i>what</i> he's thinking.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:33.200
Oh, you're home early today.

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.390
And that's the plan for the next event.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.440
If you have any questions, please ask.

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:11.400
Okay.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:15.530
We'll be going, then.

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:16.900
...Um...

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:26.000
How did you feel
about your first performance?

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:35.060
When I was on stage,
my mind went blank.

00:08:35.060 --> 00:08:37.210
It took everything I had just to sing.

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:40.760
But when we finish singing,

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.230
we receive applause.

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:49.520
And when I thought that
this was our first step, I was overjoyed.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:54.040
...But now we're in a bit of a pickle...

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.280
We do not know what to be doing.

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.040
Oh good, your fever's gone down.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.570
Rest up today, okay?

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:13.190
Rin must be worried.

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.660
Mio went today.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:19.890
I know it.

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.580
What is it, Mama?

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:31.540
How are you feeling?

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.190
I'm sorry for the sudden visit.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:44.210
I intended only to
leave you a get-well snack,

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:45.870
...but, um...

00:09:46.420 --> 00:09:48.840
your mother insisted that I visit.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.880
...U-Um...

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:53.380
I'll leave it by the door.

00:09:55.220 --> 00:09:56.910
Do take care.

00:09:57.670 --> 00:09:59.800
P-Producer!

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:03.270
...U-Um...

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:05.520
Could you wait downstairs?

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.780
I'll be there in a minute.

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:14.110
I'm so sorry.

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:17.110
I just had to catch a cold
at a time like this.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:23.100
Don't worry about it.

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:25.870
Is she idoling as well as she says?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:28.410
Yes.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.340
She was so nervous
about her concert the other day,

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:35.280
she wouldn't stop practicing
for a single second!

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:36.370
...And then she—

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.570
M-Mama!

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.760
You don't need to tell everyone!

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:41.930
Enjoy!

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:48.940
...Mama likes to talk a lot...

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:56.490
Are you sick too, Producer?

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.150
Huh?

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:00.770
You seem a bit under the weather.

00:11:01.860 --> 00:11:02.530
No.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:13.510
What kind of work
are we going to get next?

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:17.720
...Shimamura...

00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:20.770
What would you like to happen next?

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:27.100
Well, I always wanted to
stand on stage, and we got to do that.

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:30.980
And we already released a single,
...and went on the radio...

00:11:33.030 --> 00:11:36.290
It would be great
if we could get on TV next!

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:40.740
...Um...

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:44.180
...Actually, about our mini-concert...

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:48.360
There's one thing I regret.

00:11:49.990 --> 00:11:52.790
I finally got to stand on stage,

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:57.140
but I couldn't smile
through the whole concert.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:11:59.050
Huh?

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:05.730
So the next time I go on stage,
I want to smile the entire time.

00:12:05.730 --> 00:12:08.470
With Rin and Mio!

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.480
...I'm sure I'll be better tomor—

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.780
Please rest well.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:20.140
Okay.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.500
Producer!

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.530
I look forward to working
with you again tomorrow!

00:12:43.880 --> 00:12:46.130
P-Producer!

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:48.390
Tell us.

00:12:49.010 --> 00:12:51.070
What's going to happen to the project?

00:12:51.070 --> 00:12:53.390
And Mio? And Rin?

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.430
Are they really quitting?

00:12:55.430 --> 00:12:57.740
The beginning of the end begins.

00:12:56.260 --> 00:12:59.640
It's really turning into a mess.

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:00.900
...We...

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:05.250
We decided to wait and believe.

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:08.160
But... But now what?

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:09.410
It will be fine.

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:14.360
New Generations will not break up.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.250
No one is quitting.

00:13:18.020 --> 00:13:19.050
I guarantee you.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:23.630
I will bring them back.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:25.990
...So...

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.140
Please wait.

00:13:43.980 --> 00:13:44.700
Hello!

00:13:44.700 --> 00:13:46.550
How's everyone doing?

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:50.450
...Um... We're...

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:53.700
...waiting for our producer....

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:59.670
Maybe I can tell a story while we wait, then.

00:14:00.380 --> 00:14:02.000
A story?

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:02.670
Yes.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:09.320
Once upon a time, in a faraway land,

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:12.850
there lived a very straightforward man.

00:14:13.480 --> 00:14:16.900
He would always chart a clear,
straight path for his Cinderellas to walk.

00:14:16.900 --> 00:14:18.850
Straight on, straight up.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:29.110
But sometimes, when your path is clear
and straight, you can feel a little suffocated.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:35.740
And so, some of his Cinderellas left him.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:41.750
After that, the man grew very timid

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:51.470
and transformed into a quiet carriage, which would
only take Cinderellas to the foot of the castle.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.090
...Is that...

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.930
...Producer's story?...

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:07.530
Now, let's wait a little longer to
see if the spell will break tonight.

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:14.740
Sorry, Shimamu.

00:15:16.340 --> 00:15:18.320
I'm a failure as a leader.

00:15:33.230 --> 00:15:35.140
Wait, my balcony?!

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:40.690
Why?

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:45.150
...After everything I said...

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:48.090
...Wha— Wait—

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:54.030
I'm so sorry. I mistook you for a pervert.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:01.770
Bye.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.030
Please wait.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.790
I told you I quit.

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:23.680
Honda!

00:16:25.060 --> 00:16:29.130
Please... give me one chance to talk it over.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:34.860
...Are these...

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:37.970
Photographs from your concert.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:41.490
What the heck?

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:44.100
I'm not smiling in any of these.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.710
When I said the results were only natural,

00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:52.680
I did not mean that
it would naturally be a failure.

00:16:53.650 --> 00:16:56.220
I believe it was a success.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.470
How?

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.370
No one even came.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.410
Look at the next picture.

00:17:12.730 --> 00:17:15.860
I like these smiles.

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:21.120
Yes, excluding friends
and family, not many came.

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:25.780
However, these people
stopped and took a moment

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:28.250
just to hear you sing.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:39.610
...They even clapped...

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:41.570
I'm such an idiot.

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:44.650
...No, I failed—

00:17:44.650 --> 00:17:48.440
You know... I was only
looking at the numbers.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:53.270
I see now.

00:17:53.270 --> 00:17:55.400
It wasn't a failure.

00:17:57.850 --> 00:18:00.990
But that makes it even worse!

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:05.220
I was an idiot and ruined the whole concert!

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:07.890
...And I...

00:18:08.740 --> 00:18:10.350
I ran away!

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:12.750
...I'm the leader...

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:15.010
I'm terrible!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:21.010
Honda, please come back.

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:26.160
What am I supposed to say to them?

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:29.680
...I caused so much trouble for everyone...

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:34.840
I think that is all the
more reason to face them.

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:42.030
I cannot allow myself to lose any of you.

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:18.250
It's a brand new evolu revolu generation.

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.840
...Hello there, everyo—

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.370
Shiburin!

00:19:35.310 --> 00:19:36.210
Mio?

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:38.670
Producer?

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.450
...Shiburin, I...

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:48.750
I'm sorry!

00:19:50.460 --> 00:19:54.290
I'm sorry for saying I was quitting!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.890
And for running out when I was leader!

00:19:56.890 --> 00:19:58.350
And for making you worry!

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.190
I'm sorry!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:05.400
But I don't want it to end like this!

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:09.580
I want to keep being an idol with you!

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:16.410
Shibuya.

00:20:19.010 --> 00:20:24.190
Like you said,
I may have been running away.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:29.360
From facing you all directly.

00:20:31.700 --> 00:20:36.250
I caused you distress and hurt you.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:41.200
I'm tired.

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:45.500
I still don't know what idols are.

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:48.950
I didn't know even when I started.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:52.750
I've come this far, and I still don't know.

00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:56.370
I don't want this anymore.

00:20:57.390 --> 00:21:01.240
I don't know who to trust when I'm lost.

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:05.760
I'm tired of all this.

00:21:13.110 --> 00:21:14.390
I will do my best.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:19.010
So that you can trust me again.

00:21:31.130 --> 00:21:32.200
Shiburin!

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:38.670
Let's try searching once more

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.260
for something you can devote yourself to.

00:21:49.930 --> 00:21:53.130
I look forward to
working with you tomorrow.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:55.130
Okay!

00:21:57.140 --> 00:22:03.020
It was so beautiful, so dreamlike, that I nearly cried

00:22:03.020 --> 00:22:09.110
That shooting star I saw streaming as the sun set

00:22:03.340 --> 00:22:04.790
We're sorry!

00:22:06.700 --> 00:22:09.950
Rin! Mio!

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:12.950
I'm so happy!

00:22:12.950 --> 00:22:14.080
Sorry.

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:18.790
I just love it when the sky is dyed in twilight

00:22:17.400 --> 00:22:22.150
Thank you very much for waiting.

00:22:18.790 --> 00:22:25.050
And I love collecting together miracles

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:28.220
I hope that this will mark the beginning
of a new chapter in the Cinderella Project.

00:22:25.050 --> 00:22:29.720
Everyone has a story

00:22:29.120 --> 00:22:33.220
We will climb the stairway to the
castle together, one step at a time.

00:22:29.720 --> 00:22:36.560
Walk your own path; you can start at any time

00:22:33.650 --> 00:22:34.970
Okay!

00:22:36.560 --> 00:22:48.070
Look, the sunset's gentle glow is its present to you

00:22:38.410 --> 00:22:39.850
Hey, Producer, idea for you!

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:43.300
Could you try to stop talking like a robot?

00:22:43.300 --> 00:22:43.860
Huh?

00:22:44.280 --> 00:22:47.210
Yeah, it makes it kinda hard to talk to mew.

00:22:47.210 --> 00:22:49.450
The time has come to lay waste to the wall?

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:53.530
It was so beautiful, so dreamlike, that I nearly cried

00:22:49.780 --> 00:22:52.780
I think tha's a goo' i'ea!

00:22:53.070 --> 00:22:54.720
Me too! Me too!

00:22:53.530 --> 00:22:59.290
And there's plenty to look forward to as well

00:22:54.720 --> 00:22:56.410
I'd like that too!

00:22:56.790 --> 00:23:00.260
...Um, I think, um, that would...

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:04.670
Will I be able to reach it if I stretch out my hand?

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:02.040
...make it easier to talk to you....

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:07.550
I will tr— I'll try... my best.

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:10.740
That shooting star I saw streaming as the sun set

00:23:10.340 --> 00:23:15.600
Will I be able to touch it if I stretch out my hand?

00:23:10.590 --> 00:23:11.980
So, what should we do first?

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:13.940
We await your guidance.

00:23:12.820 --> 00:23:14.150
Why not go in?

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:21.350
The gentle flower petals dancing in the wind

00:23:15.720 --> 00:23:18.310
It's not really my place, so no thanks.

00:23:21.350 --> 00:23:25.270
Like all our dreams

00:23:35.650 --> 00:23:38.560
I can't wait for our next time on stage.

00:23:42.740 --> 00:23:44.080
You've got a one-track mind, Uzuki.

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:47.090
And, no joke, it makes you kinda cool.

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.040
H-Huh?

00:23:51.170 --> 00:23:53.650
All right. Let's do this.

00:23:54.460 --> 00:23:58.300
Fried chicken!
